---
import ProseLayout from '../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const ads = !!site.adsenseClient;
const form = !!site.contactEndpoint;
---

<ProseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  lead={`How ${site.name} handles information when you use the site.`}
  description={`The ${site.name} privacy policy: what information is collected, how it is used and the choices you have.`}
  updated={site.legalUpdated}
>
  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Summary:</strong> you can use every simulation without an account. {
        ads
          ? 'We show ads from Google, which uses cookies as described below.'
          : 'We do not currently use analytics, advertising or tracking cookies.'
      } The only thing the site stores on your device is your light or dark theme choice.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Information stored on your device</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} saves your theme preference (light or dark) in your browser’s <em>local storage</em> under the key
    <code>veylora-theme</code>, so the site looks the way you chose on your next visit. This value never leaves your
    device and is not sent to us. You can remove it at any time by clearing your browser’s site data.
  </p>
  {
    !ads && (
      <p>
        {site.name} itself does not set cookies, run analytics scripts or include advertising technology at this time.
      </p>
    )
  }

  <h2>2. Information you send us</h2>
  <p>
    If you contact us, we receive the name, email address and message you provide. We use this only to read and reply
    to your message, and we do not sell it or use it for marketing.
    {
      form
        ? ' Messages sent with the contact form are delivered to us through a third-party form-processing service, which processes them on our behalf.'
        : ' If you write to us by email, your message is handled by our email provider.'
    }
  </p>
  <p>We keep messages only as long as needed to respond and to keep a record of corrections or suggestions.</p>

  <h2>3. Server logs</h2>
  <p>
    Like almost every website, the company that hosts {site.name} may automatically record technical information when
    pages are requested, such as your IP address, browser type and the page visited. These logs are used for security
    and to keep the site running, and are retained according to the hosting provider’s policies.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Fonts and third-party requests</h2>
  <p>
    Fonts and other assets are served from our own site, so loading a page does not send your information to font or
    content-delivery services.{ads && ' The exception is the advertising code described below.'}
  </p>

  <h2>5. Advertising</h2>
  {
    ads ? (
      <>
        <p>
          {site.name} uses Google AdSense to display advertisements, which helps keep the site free.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website or other websites.</li>
          <li>
            Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visit to
            this site and/or other sites on the internet.
          </li>
          <li>
            You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting{' '}
            <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>. You can also opt out of
            some third-party vendors’ use of cookies for personalized advertising at{' '}
            <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">www.aboutads.info</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            Learn more in{' '}
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">
              How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services
            </a>
            .
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland are asked for consent before
          personalized advertising cookies are used.
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <p>
        {site.name} does not currently display advertising. We may introduce advertising (for example Google AdSense)
        in the future to help keep the site free. If we do, we will update this policy <strong>before</strong> any ads
        appear, including how advertising cookies are used and how you can opt out.
      </p>
    )
  }

  <h2>6. Children’s privacy</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} is designed to be used by learners of all ages, including children, without creating an account or
    sharing personal information. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you are
    under 13, please ask a parent, guardian or teacher to contact us on your behalf. If you believe a child has sent us
    personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct or delete personal information we hold about
    you, such as a message you sent us. To make a request, use our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Simulator pages link to textbooks and other external references. Those sites have their own privacy policies, and
    we are not responsible for their practices.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page whenever our practices change — for example, if we add analytics or advertising — and
    change the “last updated” date above.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy? Reach us through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</ProseLayout>
